  "rawBulletin": "REGIONAL SPECIALISED METEOROLOGICAL CENTRE -TROPICAL CYCLONES,\nNEW DELHI TROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO 09\nDEMS-RSMC TROPICAL CYCLONES NEW DELHI DATED 17.11.2026\nFROM: RSMC \u2013TROPICAL CYCLONES, NEW DELHI\nTO: STORM WARNING CENTRE, NAYPYITAW (MYANMAR)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, BANGKOK (THAILAND)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, COLOMBO (SRILANKA)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, DHAKA (BANGLADESH)\nSTORM WARNING CENTRE, KARACHI (PAKISTAN)\nMETEOROLOGICAL OFFICE, MALE (MALDIVES)\nOMAN METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT,\nMUSCAT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nYEMEN METEOROLOGICAL SERVICES,\nREPUBLIC OF YEMEN (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nNATIONAL CENTRE FOR METEOROLOGY, UAE (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nPRESIDENCY OF METEOROLOGY AND ENVIRONMENT,\nSAUDI ARABIA (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nIRAN METEOROLOGICAL ORGANISATION, (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nQATAR METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (THROUGH RTH JEDDAH)\nTROPICAL CYCLONE ADVISORY NO. 09 FOR THE NORTH INDIAN OCEAN\n(THE BAY OF BENGAL AND THE ARABIAN SEA) VALID FOR THE NEXT 168\nHOURS ISSUED AT 1630 UTC OF 17.11.2026 BASED ON 1200 UTC OF\n17.11.2026.\nSub: Cyclonic Storm Akvan (pronounced a Akvan) over central parts of South\nand adjoining Westcentral Bay of Bengal\nThe Cyclonic Storm \u201cAkvan\u201d [Pronunciation: Akvan] over central parts of South and\nadjoining Westcentral Bay of Bengal remained practically stationary during past 03 hours\nand lay centered at 1200 UTC of today, the 17th November, 2026 over the same region,\nnear Latitude 12.3\u00b0N and Longitude 85.6\u00b0E, about 590 km east of Chennai (43279, Tamil\nNadu), 630 km northeast of Trincomalee (43418, Sri Lanka), 650 km southeast of\nMachilipatnam (43185, Andhra Pradesh), 650 km south-southeast of Visakhapatnam\n(43149, Andhra Pradesh) and 780 km south of Gopalpur (43049, Odisha).\nIt is very likely to move slowly north-northwestwards and intensify further into a Severe\nCyclonic Storm over westcentral Bay of Bengal around 0000 UTC of 18th November.\nThereafter, it is likely to move northwestwards and intensify further into a very severe\ncyclonic storm around 1200 UTC of 19th November, 2026.\nCloud distribution: (a) Isolated: <25%, Scattered:25-50%, Broken: 51-75%, Solid:>75%, Convection Intensity: (a) Weak:\nCloud Top Temperature(CTT)>-25\u00b0C, (b) Moderate: CTT:-25\u00b0Cto-40\u00b0C, (c) Intense: CTT: -41\u00b0Cto -70\u00b0C and (d) Very\nIntense::Less than -70\u00b0C Probability of cyclogenesis (formation of depression) :NIL:0%, LOW:1-33%, MODERATE:34-\n66% and HIGH:67-100%\nContinuing to move northwestward, it is likely to cross Andhra Pradesh & Yanam coasts\nbetween Nellore and Visakhapatnam, around 0600 UTC of 20th November, 2026 as a very\nsevere cyclonic storm with the maximum sustained wind speed of 120-130 kmph gusting to\n145 kmph.\nThe forecast location and intensity of the system is given below:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(UTC) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n17.11.26/1200 12.3/85.6 75-85 gusting to 95 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/1800 12.5/85.5 85-95 gusting to 105 Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/0000 12.7/85.4 90-100 gusting to 110 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/0600 13.1/85.2 95-105 gusting to 115 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/1200 13.5/85.0 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/0000 14.2/84.5 110-120 gusting to 130 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/1200 15.1/83.8 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n20.11.26/0000 16.1/82.9 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n20.11.26/0600 16.9/82.4 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n20.11.26/1200 17.6/82.0 60-70 gusting to 80 Cyclonic Storm\n21.11.26/0000 18.4/81.7 40-50 gusting to 60 Depression\n21.11.26/1200 19.5/81.7 25-35 gusting to 45 Well Marked Low Pressure\nArea\nAs per INSAT 3DS, vortex lay over the Central parts of South Bay and adjoining\nWestcentral Bay of Bengal and its neighbourhood centered near 12.3N/85.7 E. Intensity of\nthe system is characterized as T2.5. The System shows share pattern. The convective\ncloud are sheared towards northwest from the LLCC. Associated scattered to broken low\nand medium-level clouds, ",
